== Fixed stages, samples and controls
#text("One fresh constructor run RUN-ISOU-bdbf5d, then one fresh independent verification RUN-ISOU-2b2372 only after constructor exit0/statusCONSTRUCTED and a sealed certificate. All filesystem arguments are absolute. Neither existing output may be replaced, and no retry/adaptive exponent is included. Constructor success alone is not verification. Fresh verify binds the precise certificate hash and must not reuse a producer verification verdict.")
#parbreak()
#text("The point set is exactly8 deterministic public inputs: O,G,−G,[2]G,[3]G,[17]G,[101]G,[65537]G. They are fixed known-answer inputs, not unseen random targets. Full point coordinates, infinity handling, geometric and subgroup evaluator agreement, both dual compositions, curve membership and group-law compatibility are checked. Point agreement does not prove degree. No expanded kernel or rational-map polynomial is promised by this category.")
#parbreak()
#text("The committed focused implementation controls cover exponent3/degree7, exponent5/31, exponent7/127; prime exponent11 with composite M11=2047; composite exponent9; and declared handling of exponent2. They must also cover beta=1, wrong beta/lambda pairing, norm/source/identity/hash/recurrence mutations, and the degree alias alpha+[n]. The alias keeps rational-point outputs but must fail the original norm-degree certificate. An identity coefficient changed by2^61−1 must fail the exact integer checker even if finite-field evaluation cannot distinguish it. The protocol binds those receipts; it does not silently rerun an unbounded control grid during the scientific instance.")
