== Machine protection and full cost accounting
#text("Constructor wall watchdog1800s, fresh verify3600s, sampled worker RSS8GiB per phase, certificate input2MiB, post-run serialized output admission limit256MiB, at most one scientific process for this goal, and no unaccounted worker. Native worker sampling is25ms; preserve the actual receipt and label it sampled rather than true continuous peak. The supervisor is a separate process; its own resource use is reported where measured rather than claiming an unmeasured total-tree peak. Monitoring unavailable beyond the native100ms grace, a lost process or absent terminal receipt makes the attempt INCOMPLETE. Brief unavailable samples inside that recorded grace remain explicit in the receipt. Only one computational worker is authorized. If an implementation adds multiple workers, a new resource-binding amendment must define and enforce combined RSS before launch. Watchdog limits protect this host; they do not cap campaign spending or prove mathematical impossibility. Retain stdout/stderr and partial outputs when any limit trips.")
#parbreak()
#text("Report total constructor and independent-verifier wall/CPU/RSS/bytes separately, including all LL, Cornacchia, coefficient, identity and point work inside their phase totals. If individual internal timings are unavailable, report them as unavailable and do not invent a component breakdown. Charge failed attempts as well. Retain command/cwd, UTC start/end, host/OS/CPU, source/binary/input/output hashes, status/exit/signal, watchdog sample receipt and directory manifest. Native elapsed_ms_operational_only is descriptive; the native supervised terminal receipt supplies the worker phase boundary; record outer command wall/CPU separately where available. No performance comparison or speedup is predeclared.")
